  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected metadata type and field identities, static field offset, string literals, code windows, and direct call/jump instructions.",
    "direct": "EntityDataStorage.CreateEnemyFromServer passes its Proto.SCENE_MONSTER argument to EnemyInfo.InitFromServerData. That method reads SCENE_MONSTER.commonInfo.templateid for an EnemyTable lookup, then passes the same SCENE_MONSTER to EnemyServerData's message constructor. The constructor copies commonInfo.templateid into EnemyServerData.enemyId and EnemyInfo stores it as BaseEntityData.serverData. On the checked EntityNode spawn path, EntityNode.data.serverData is passed through typed ObjectContainer.SpawnEntity and LoadEntity arguments to Entity.AssignServerData, which stores Entity.serverData. EnemyRootComponent.InitSelf copies EnemyServerData.enemyId from Entity.serverData into EnemyRootComponent.enemyId. On the unpatched synchronous EnemyAIComponent initialization path, the inherited BaseComponent.entity points to Entity.enemy; its enemyId is the key passed to Tables.s_enemyTable. A successful lookup supplies an EnemyData bean. The code reads the same bean field selected by EnemyData.get_aiTemplateId, formats the AIConfig path from that string, and passes the path to LoadSingleConfig before storing the returned EnemyAIConfigData.",
    "conditional": "The route requires a nonnull Proto.SCENE_MONSTER.commonInfo, successful EnemyTable lookup and template setup, selection of the resulting EnemyInfo into an EntityNode, its checked spawn path, an EnemyServerData cast, and nonempty aiTemplateId; IFix may redirect methods. These are static native branches, not a witnessed message, enemy instance, resource load, or graph execution.",
    "unresolved": "The source and selection of a live Proto.SCENE_MONSTER message, relation of installed spawn or scene records to that message, selection of an EnemyInfo into a particular EntityNode, use of the alternate EnemyServerData(string,int) constructor, async and override paths, and live graph instance are not established by this contract."
  },
